                                                  \begin{document}$$f\left({x}_{i,j}\right)$$\end{document}fxi,j (Equation 2) contains several tunable parameters:  Ti is the life-time of node i, ni,j, the Hill coefficient of the interaction between nodes i and j, and ki,j is the strength of the regulation of node j on i. If ki,j=0, no regulation is present and the higher the value, the stronger the regulation. For this study, n was fixed at 3, while τ and k were bounded between 0 and 1 (Eduati et al, 2017; Wittmann et al, 2009). As every node has a distinct τ value and each edge a k value, this means that the number of parameters to be estimated scales with the PKN size (number of proteins and interactions). For the curated CXCL9 PKN, this corresponds to 33 τ and 61 k parameters to be optimized. The initial activities of simulated proteins were set at 0.5 to allow for both up and down regulation, except for CXCL9, which was set to 0 as no downregulation was observed experimentally.1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
